    <tr>
        <td width="684" height="50" colspan="2">
            <p align="center"><font size="4"><b>Manufacturing Process</b></font><font size="4"><b> : Printing Section</b></font></p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td width="684" height="2" colspan="2">            <hr>
</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td width="270" height="2">
            <p align="center"><img src="img/printing_1.jpg" width="200" height="148" border="0"></p>
        </td>
        <td width="414" height="2">
            <p><font size="3"><b>◈</b></font><b><font size="3"> Copperplate Procuction Process</font></b></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;When putting the resin to the hopper, it moves&nbsp;forward</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; by&nbsp;the screw and is heated and melted.&nbsp;When the air is</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; blown to the resin that is melted and&nbsp;pushed, the film of</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; tube type&nbsp;is produced. This&nbsp;process cuts the both sides</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; of the film of tube type&nbsp;to make it flat, winds it in the</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; roll type and produces&nbsp;the
biaxial orientation film.</font></p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td width="684" height="2" colspan="2">            <hr>
</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td width="270" height="2">
            <p align="center"><img src="img/printing_2.jpg" width="200" height="143" border="0"></p>
        </td>
        <td width="414" height="2">
            <p><font size="3"><b>◈</b></font><b><font size="3"> Film Process</font></b></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;When the production of copperplate finishes, the&nbsp;proof</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; press prints for test before main printing. This&nbsp;process is</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; the test printing to check whether there is&nbsp;any mistake</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; in color, omission or misprint or whether&nbsp;it observes the</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; requirements of &nbsp;customers and to get approval from</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; customers. </font></p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td width="684" height="2" colspan="2">            <hr>
</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td width="270" height="2">
            <p align="center"><img src="img/printing_3.jpg" width="200" height="143" border="0"></p>
        </td>
        <td width="414" height="2">
            <p><font size="3"><b>◈</b></font><b><font size="3"> Gravure Printing Process</font></b></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Refers to the method of Gravure printing, one type&nbsp;of</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; intaglio&nbsp;printing. This process applies the ink to&nbsp;the</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; copperplate for printing that was engraved&nbsp;(etching),</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; gives pressure to the ink which remains in&nbsp;the etched</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; parts after removing the ink on the&nbsp;surface of </font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;copperplate so that it can be transferred&nbsp;to the&nbsp;textile</font></p>
            <p><font size="2">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;( film, paper, etc. )</font></p>
        </td>
    </tr>
